  "tagline": "A priority queue of jobs for the robots: routing by tool, stages with dependencies, and no duplicates.",
  "description": "HYDRA-UMC-JOB-DISPATCHER keeps a global queue of jobs, orders it by priority and hands each job to a robot that registered the tool the job names. Jobs have stages with dependencies and a duplicate-proof submission key; a robot that falls silent stops receiving work. The queue lives in memory or, with -db, in a pure-Go SQLite file. The HTTP surface needs a Bearer token outside the loopback address.",
